          "unit_id": "radio_interview",
          "title": "On the Radio",
          "description": "Habla de probabilidades y planes como en una entrevista: bound to, likely to, set to, due to, on the verge of.",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "lesson_id": "radio_interview_lesson",
              "title": "Talking about likelihood",
              "steps": [
                {
                  "phase": "context",
                  "type": "audio_context",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "On the radio",
                    "dialogue": [
                      {
                        "speaker": "Interviewer",
                        "text": "Green Door Design is barely a year old, and yet you're about to open an office in Madrid. How did that happen?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Partly luck, partly hard work. We were lucky to find the right partners early on."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Interviewer",
                        "text": "The Madrid office is due to open in October. Is it on schedule?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "It is. We're set to hire four designers there by the end of the year."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Interviewer",
                        "text": "Are you likely to move to Madrid yourself?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "I'm unlikely to move permanently. Bristol is home now. But I'm bound to spend a lot of time on planes."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Interviewer",
                        "text": "Some say small studios are on the verge of disappearing because of AI tools. Do you agree?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "I don't think so. Good design is bound to need people who listen. Tools can help, but they don't understand a client's fears."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Interviewer",
                        "text": "What are your chances of winning the Bristol Business Award this year?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "We stand a fairly good chance, I'm told. But honestly, I'd be just as happy without it."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Interviewer",
                        "text": "Finally, any advice for someone arriving in a new city, as you did three years ago?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Say yes to everything, carry an umbrella, and never keep your keys in the fridge."
                      }
                    ],
                    "passage": "August. Lucía is being interviewed on a Bristol radio programme about small businesses."
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "discovery",
                  "type": "multiple_choice",
                  "content": {
